              "data_source_ref" : "ds_8c1e6b664bde4c23989d91bb0b8f3562",
              "id" : "viz_2ed2592238bb4ff388190c748b32313f",
              "layer" : 1,
              "options" : {
                "content" : "## why row 10 charts and row 9 doesn't\n\n**Row 9 (pivot)** ate both categorical columns to create wide column names. There's nothing left for the chart's X-axis.\n\n**Row 10 keeps the long form**:\n\n```tql\nstats avg(cpu_percent) as avg_cpu by region, role\n```\n\nThree columns — `region`, `role`, `avg_cpu` — and the strip assigns:\n\n- **X (time)**: `region`\n- **Series**: `avg_cpu`\n- **Dimension**: `role`\n\nThe chart pivots internally on the dimension. One bar per role, grouped by region. Pivot is for tables; **dimensions are for charts**.\n\n> Rule of thumb: keep the pipeline as long-form for charts. The chart's role strip does the wide-shaping at render time.",
                "content_type" : "markdown"
              },
              "type" : "text",
              "width" : 12
            }
